 "B_statement": "Flat GR + scalar: Hdot = -(1/2) phidot^2 - ... <= 0 and rho > 0, so H never changes sign: the oscillation is a ripple in addot/a, not a bounce. Hubble friction alone gives amplitudes ~ a^(-3/2) ~ 1/t: peak ratios exp(-3 pi H/m) -> 1 as H/m falls (power law, not geometric 0.7^n); a geometric sequence needs a constant damping rate (decay width): ratio exp(-pi Gamma/m).",
